  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "This is the blast furnace reaction.&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mtext>Fe</mtext><mover><mo>&#8594;</mo><mrow><mi>dilute</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mo>H</mo><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>SO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow></mover><msub><mi>FeSO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mover><mo>&#8594;</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>SO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mover><msub><mi>Fe</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mfenced><msub><mi>SO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mfenced><mn>3</mn></msub><mover><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi>heat</mi></mover><mi>Fe</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mtext>Fe</mtext><mover><mo>&#8594;</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>heat</mi></mrow></mover><mi>FeO</mi><mover><mo>&#8594;</mo><mrow><mi>dilute</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mo>H</mo><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>SO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow></mover><msub><mi>FeSO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mover><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi>heat</mi></mover><mi>Fe</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> cannot be the answer&nbsp;since, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>FeSO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math> on heating gives <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>FeO</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>SO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>.<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>Fe</mi><mover><mo>&#8594;</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Cl</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>heat</mi></mrow></mover><msub><mi>FeCl</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mover><mo>&#8594;</mo><mrow><mi>heat</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>air</mi></mrow></mover><msub><mi>FeCl</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mover><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi>Zn</mi></mover><mi>Fe</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> is wrong because <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>FeCl</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math>, on heating in air, stays as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Fe</mi><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></math> and does not form <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>FeCl</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>.",
